# dsv41: display-reserve KV, E-Zou Shen's (ezoushen) patch 0007-display-kv from
# MiaAI-Lab/DeepSeek-v4.1-Flash-1017-2x-DGX-Sparks#9, ported onto 0008's pool and window and the port's KV sharding.
# With TF_DS_DISPLAY_KV_MIB (whole 16 MiB steps up to 2032; unset or 0 is off and changes nothing) the KV caches go on
# the framebuffer a headless GB10 reserves at boot (UEFI, about 1.75 GiB a GPU), through a DRM dumb buffer on
# TF_DS_DISPLAY_KV_CARD (default /dev/dri/card0; refused when an output is connected) mapped above host pages in one
# cuMemHostRegister'd span, so those bytes leave the host's MemAvailable. The tensors that fit go there, the rest stay
# on host pages; every tensor lies wholly on one half of the span.
# - display.zig is #9's as written (a port of the DRM-framebuffer backend of the TensorFold GLM engine,
#   glm_cuda/cuda_display_kv.zig, by the TensorFold contributors). Caches.layout and Model.makeCaches are ported by
#   hand: with TF_DS_KV_SHARD=1 the layout takes this rank's owner planes (its part's compressed codes and scales) last,
#   after every layer's index keys and raw stores, so the framebuffer fills with the owner planes first; replicated,
#   the order is the arena's, as #9 places it. Each rank logs at start how many MiB went to the reserve (and of its
#   owner planes) and how many to normal memory.
# - RoPE: a stream's positions are its own (from 0 at its extent's base), so the tables need an extent plus a round's
#   rows (0008's ropeRows), never the pool or a part. A window the kit's tables (1,114,112 positions) do not cover is
#   now refused at start with the table size and the longest window that fits, instead of a bare ShortRopeTable.
# Recipe settings DISPLAY_KV_MIB and DISPLAY_KV_CARD (both ranks; start.sh also gives the containers the card node).
# Measured in #9 on the stock recipe (replicated KV, 893 MiB a rank, all of it on the framebuffer): the head's idle
# MemAvailable from 6.76 to 7.49 GiB, its lowest during a cold 96K-token prompt from 5.89 to 7.12 GiB; tools/exact.py
# 31 of 31 identical with it on and off. Measured on this pair with the port's sharded pool, at POOL=5218304 and
# DISPLAY_KV_MIB=1792: 1,791 MiB a rank on the reserve (all of its owner planes), 852 MiB in normal memory; exact.py
# 39 of 39 identical; the lowest MemAvailable during a 227,640-token prompt 6.57 / 8.32 GiB, against 6.44 / 8.22 GiB
# for 2,101,248 positions without the reserve.
# Applies after 0023 (engine port/series-display-kv-pair-370daf0: one commit on port/series-pair-370daf0).
# display.zig by E-Zou Shen (@ezoushen); its wiring onto the pool and window and KV sharding by Robert Wojciechowski
# (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo). Apache-2.0.
